.TH SOCKET 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
Socket \- low-level Berkeley socket API for TCP/UDP networking
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBSocket\fR module provides low-level TCP/UDP socket programming via the POSIX Berkeley socket API.
.PP
The module exposes the following socket-type and protocol constants: 
AF_INET, AF_INET6, SOCK_STREAM, SOCK_DGRAM, SOCK_RAW, IPPROTO_TCP, IPPROTO_UDP, SOL_SOCKET, SO_REUSEADDR, SO_BROADCAST. 
These are numeric constants matching the platform's socket.h values.
.PP
Socket objects returned by \fBSocket.create()\fR are \fBSocketObj\fR instances with the following methods: bind, listen, accept, connect, send, recv, close, setblocking, setsockopt.
.SH EXAMPLES
Import examples:
.nf
import Socket
.fi
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS create
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
SocketObj() Socket.create(domain: int(), type: int(), protocol: int())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Creates a socket using the POSIX socket() syscall (::socket on POSIX, ::socket on Windows).
.TP
\fBARGUMENTS\fR
\fBdomain\fR (int()) \- Address family (AF_INET, AF_INET6, etc.).
.br
\fBtype\fR (int()) \- Socket type (SOCK_STREAM, SOCK_DGRAM, SOCK_RAW).
.br
\fBprotocol\fR (int()) \- Protocol (IPPROTO_TCP, IPPROTO_UDP, or 0 for auto).
.TP
\fBRETURN VALUE\fR
SocketObj() \- A socket instance.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR \- if called with fewer than 3 arguments.
.br
\fBRuntimeError\fR \- if socket creation fails.
.TP
\fBEXAMPLES\fR
.nf
s = Socket.create(AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM, IPPROTO_TCP)
s.connect("127.0.0.1", 8080)
s.send("GET / HTTP/1.0\\r\\n\\r\\n")
resp = s.recv(4096)
s.close()
.fi
.SH "SOCKETOBJ METHODS"
.TP
\fBbind(host: string(), port: int())\fR
Binds the socket to the given host and port using AF_INET/sockaddr_in. 
The host is converted via inet_addr (dotted-decimal string).
.br
\fBErrors:\fR \fBArgumentError\fR \- fewer than 4 total args (self + dummy + host + port).
.TP
\fBlisten(backlog: int())\fR
Marks the socket as a passive server socket willing to accept up to backlog queued connections.
.br
\fBErrors:\fR \fBArgumentError\fR \- fewer than 3 total args (self + dummy + backlog).
.TP
\fBaccept()\fR -> SocketObj()
Accepts a pending connection on a listening socket.
.br
\fBErrors:\fR \fBRuntimeError\fR \- if ::accept() fails.
.TP
\fBconnect(host: string(), port: int())\fR
Connects the socket to the remote address host:port.
.br
\fBErrors:\fR \fBArgumentError\fR \- fewer than 4 total args.
.TP
\fBsend(data: string())\fR -> int()
Sends data over the socket.
.br
\fBErrors:\fR \fBArgumentError\fR \- fewer than 3 total args.
.TP
\fBrecv(size: int())\fR -> string()
Receives up to size bytes from the socket.
.br
\fBErrors:\fR \fBArgumentError\fR \- fewer than 3 total args.
.TP
\fBclose()\fR
Closes the socket.
.TP
\fBsetblocking(blocking: bool())\fR
Sets the socket to blocking (true) or non-blocking (false) mode. 
On POSIX uses fcntl F_GETFL/F_SETFL with O_NONBLOCK. 
On Windows uses ioctlsocket with FIONBIO.
.br
\fBErrors:\fR \fBArgumentError\fR \- fewer than 3 total args.
.TP
\fBsetsockopt(level: int(), optname: int(), value: int())\fR
Sets a socket option.
.br
\fBErrors:\fR \fBArgumentError\fR \- fewer than 5 total args (self + dummy + level + optname + value).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Http(3), Serial(3)
